# Mobile-First Responsiveness — Hilgod Online Shop

## Background
The current CSS was written **desktop-first** (base styles target wide viewports, then overridden with `max-width` media queries). This causes:
- Inconsistent breakpoints (12 different widths used: 315, 360, 420, 440, 480, 540, 576, 600, 640, 700, 768, 900, 992, 1024, 1100)
- Key layouts not collapsing on phones (filter sidebar, product catalog, checkout, admin tables)
- Font sizes, paddings, and spacing not scaling down gracefully
- No standardised breakpoint system (each file uses different values)

The goal is a **systematic mobile-first rewrite** using a single unified breakpoint scale.

---

## Unified Breakpoint Scale (Mobile-First)

| Token | Value | Devices |
|-------|-------|---------|
| `sm`  | 480px | Large phones |
| `md`  | 768px | Tablets / landscape phones |
| `lg`  | 992px | Small laptops / large tablets |
| `xl`  | 1280px | Desktops |

All `@media` rules will become `min-width` (mobile-first) instead of `max-width`.

